<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Odessa Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Odessa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bolshevik republic proclaimed in Odessa in January 1918, which lasted only until the German and Austrian advance in March.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In January 1918 Bolsheviks and their allies seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odessa">Odessa</a> after street fighting with forces of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic">Ukrainian People's Republic</a>. They proclaimed the Odessa Soviet Republic, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-yudovsky">Vladimir Yudovsky</a> as head of its council of people's commissars, claiming authority over the city and surrounding province.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic relied on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-guards-russia">Red Guards</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea-fleet">Black Sea Fleet</a> sailors, imposed levies on the wealthy and carried out arrests and executions. It also fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-romania">Kingdom of Romania</a>, which had occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a>, and reached a short-lived ceasefire agreement with it. Its control barely extended beyond the city.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</a>, Austro-Hungarian and German troops advanced on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odessa">Odessa</a>, and the Soviet leaders evacuated the city in March 1918. The republic was nominally merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukrainian-soviet-republic">Ukrainian Soviet Republic</a> and ceased to exist.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/odessa-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Odessa Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Odessa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vladimir Yudovsky</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>State atheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Odesa Soviet Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=odessa-soviet-republic" aria-label="Odessa Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5512 441 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Odessa Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5832 697L5820 533M5832 697L5380 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M5380 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5832 697h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5832 697h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=odessa-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

